 "takeaway": "A hot recent record barely moved the needle: lines that hit in 70%+ of his last 20 won 50.1%, lines under 30% won 46.1%, and every band lost money because Overs at these prices came true 47.7% of the time against an average price of 49.2\u00a2. The books' line was the best single read (Brier 0.2464); our matchup model on its own (0.2602) was worse than a coin flip until shrunk, and blending it in as Wedger % (0.2465) did not beat the price. Lines where Wedger % beat the price by 3+ points went 34 of 93. In the NBA the price is the signal; use the screen and the outlook to understand a line, not as an edge on their own."
